# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .dockerignore — keep the build context to core runtime code only.
#
# Deploy reality (verified 2026-09-13; no Dockerfile exists in the repo or in
# git history on consolidation/10 — the old pnpm-era one was deleted):
#   * Backend deploys via railway.json: buildCommand runs tsc for
#     @axiom/config, @axiom/chat-runtime, @axiom/backend; startCommand is
#     `bun apps/backend/dist/index.js`. The standalone-binary path is
#     `bun scripts/build-binaries.mjs` (bun build --compile of
#     apps/backend/src/index.ts -> dist/axiom-backend). Backend ABIs live in
#     packages/config/src/abis/*.ts — apps/contracts sources are NOT needed.
#   * Frontend is built separately by Vercel (vercel.json: --filter
#     @axiom/frontend build, outputDirectory apps/frontend/dist).
#
# A future Dockerfile must therefore provide: package.json, bun.lock,
# bunfig.toml, tsconfig.base.json (every package tsconfig extends it),
# scripts/build-binaries.mjs, apps/backend/{package.json,tsconfig.json,src},
# packages/config/**, packages/chat-runtime/** — plus every workspace
# package.json, because bun.lock pins the whole workspace graph
# (apps/backend, apps/bench, apps/contracts, apps/frontend,
# packages/chat-runtime, packages/config) and `bun install --frozen-lockfile`
# fails if any of them is missing. Those manifests are re-included below even
# where their parent directories are excluded.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Dependencies (always installed inside the image)
**/node_modules

# VCS / CI / git tooling
.git
.gitignore
.github
.husky
.turbo

# CRITICAL: secrets — must never enter a build context.
# Covers .env, .env.bak-compute-key, .env.secrets-local and nested variants
# (e.g. apps/frontend/.env.*). DECISION ON .env.example: it is excluded too —
# nothing in any build path reads it (no Dockerfile exists; the historical
# Dockerfile never COPYed it) and runtime config belongs in deploy env vars,
# not image layers. Re-add `!.env.example` below only if a future Dockerfile
# deliberately COPYs it as a template.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
# Raw key material: wallets/ holds deployer/oracle/tee-signer JSON keyfiles.
wallets
wallets/*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.secret

# AI-agent / IDE / local-tool state (not source)
.agents
.antigravitycli
.claude
.design-audit
.firecrawl
.grok
.hoplite
.impeccable
.kimchi
.omc
.vercel
.zcode

# Audit / report / docs-as-consumable output
_agent_reports
analysis_reports
frontend_analysis_reports
audit
audit-reports
report
artifacts
docs
rules
**/*.md
LICENSE

# Build outputs and test/coverage artifacts (regenerated during build)
dist
**/dist
**/coverage
**/.nyc_output
**/*.tsbuildinfo
*.log
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# Workspaces not needed for the backend image.
# frontend -> built by Vercel; contracts -> Foundry sources (ABIs the backend
# uses are TS files in packages/config/src/abis); bench -> dev benchmarking.
# Keep each workspace's package.json: bun.lock requires the full workspace
# graph. Relax the apps/contracts rule if a Foundry builder stage ever
# returns (the deleted historical Dockerfile had one and COPYed
# apps/contracts/ into it).
apps/frontend/*
!apps/frontend/package.json
apps/contracts/*
!apps/contracts/package.json
apps/bench/*
!apps/bench/package.json

# Backend sub-trees that no build step needs (safe to COPY apps/backend/
# wholesale after these):
# main tsconfig.json does not reference e2e; e2e has its own tsconfig.
apps/backend/e2e
apps/backend/tsconfig.e2e.json
apps/backend/scripts
apps/backend/data

# Runtime checkpoints at the repo root (never build input)
data

# Dev-tooling configs (linters, formatters, scanners, deploy ignores)
.gitleaks.toml
.gitmessage
.markdownlint-cli2.jsonc
.mise.toml
.prettierignore
.prettierrc.json
.railwayignore
.solhint.json
.vercelignore
eslint.config.js
sgconfig.yml
skills-lock.json
